# Always push when work is done

When a requested task is complete (feature, fix, copy, or layout):

1. Commit the relevant changes if they are not committed yet. Pushing implies commit first.
2. `git push` to the tracked remote. Do not wait to be asked again in this repo.
3. Return the remote commit URL when done.

Do not force-push `main`/`master`. Do not commit secrets, `.env`, or unrelated untracked files.
